## Defining Domain Errors

```xiom
pub type ParseError = enum {
  InvalidFormat(detail: Str),
  ValueOutOfRange(value: Int, min: Int, max: Int),
  MissingField(field_name: Str),
}

fn parse_port(input: Str) -> Result[Int, ParseError] {
  let value = input.parse_int();
  match value {
    None => return Err(ParseError::InvalidFormat("not a number")),
    Some(v) => {
      if v < 1 || v > 65535 {
        return Err(ParseError::ValueOutOfRange(v, 1, 65535));
      }
      return Ok(v);
    },
  }
}
```

### Error Type Best Practices

```xiom
pub type DbError = enum {
  ConnectionFailed(host: Str, port: Int),
  QueryFailed(query: Str, reason: Str),
  Timeout(seconds: Int),
  PermissionDenied(user: Str),
}

pub type ValidationError = enum {
  TooShort(field: Str, min_len: Int),
  TooLong(field: Str, max_len: Int),
  InvalidFormat(field: Str, expected: Str),
}
```

### Pattern Matching on Errors

```xiom
fn handle_port(config: Str) -> Int {
  match parse_port(config) {
    Ok(port) => return port,
    Err(ParseError::ValueOutOfRange(v, min, max)) => {
      io.eprintln("Port " + v.to_str() + " out of range [" + min.to_str() + "-" + max.to_str() + "]");
      return 8080;  // Default
    },
    Err(_) => return 8080,
  }
}
```

